# Companion to 2026-09-25-10.play: same cell (raid, cold, shaman:restoration,
# 25-heroic, fresh) but idle, run as its own playbot invocation. The first
# attempt put both good and idle in one script with a second `open #hash`
# mid-run to reset between pulls -- it didn't reset anything, because the app
# clears the invite hash from the address bar after reading it once, so the
# second `open #b=cold&s=25&h=1` was a fragment-only difference from the
# already-cleared current URL and Playwright (matching real browser fragment-
# navigation semantics) treated it as a same-document nav: no reload, no
# re-run of the pull. The "idle" numbers that produced were the good pull's
# own stale end-of-fight state read twice. Splitting into two invocations
# avoids the whole problem: the first navigation of a fresh browser context is
# never a fragment-only nav.
open #b=cold&s=25&h=1
targets
tap class:shaman:restoration
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot idle-open

play idle 200
bill
says
state
shot idle-end
